    - { level: 7, count: 1 }
    - { level: 10, count: 1 }
    - { level: 12, count: 1 }
extraction_notes: "Nightbane RPG printed 88-90: the package is printed 90, and the secondary skills (printed 88) and money (printed 89) are stated once on the Nightbane R.C.C. for all four packages. STORED AS A PACKAGE O.C.C. restricted to nb-nightbane, per survey D2 (PR #1124); occ_group optional follows the Heroes Unlimited Educational Level O.C.C.s. SECONDARY SKILLS are copied into each package per D2: six, plus ''an additional two at levels four and eight'', stored as two at EACH level, the reading the book''s own related-skill lines use for the same wording. ''Limited as previously indicated in the list'' is stored as this package''s related categories without bonuses. EXPERIENCE: the ''Nightbane & Guardian'' ladder, printed 233, read off a render, stored as the lower bound of each band; the top of level 15 is 600,000. MONEY: 3D6x100 in cash (printed 89); Faction funds for emergencies are prose. SKILLS: printed 90 reads ''Speak Native Language; Literacy must be selected as an other skill (+10%)''. Speaking is stored as Language: Native Tongue 98; the (+10%) is NOT stored, because a 98% skill cannot take it and the line does not say whether it belongs to a later Literacy pick, which a category bonus could not target alone. Both literacies are admitted on the Communications only-list so the book''s instruction can be followed. Tracking is the catalog''s Tracking (people). This book files Wilderness Survival under Espionage and the catalog under Wilderness, which this package does not grant, so that exclusion is enforced by the category and is not named in the Espionage except. Motorcycle is Motorcycles & Snowmobiles and motorboat is Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil (this book''s Boat: Motor and Hydrofoils). ''Physical: Any (+5% when applicable)'' is a category bonus, which a skill with no percentage does not take. HIT POINTS, S.D.C., bonuses and powers are the R.C.C.''s (printed 87-88) and are not stated here."
